fference from the mean and add it to `total_diff`.\\n\\n5. **Compute Mean Absolute Deviation (MAD)**:\\n   - Calculate the average of the absolute differences: `MAD = total_diff / len(numbers)`.\\n\\n6. **Return the Result**:\\n   - Return the computed MAD as a float.\\n\\n7. **Edge Cases**:\\n   - **Empty List**: Ensure the function returns `0.0` when the input list is empty.\\n   - **Single Element List**: Ensure the function returns `0.0` when the input list contains only one element.\\n\\n8. **Testing**:\\n   - Test the function with various inputs, including edge cases, to ensure correctness.\\n\\n9. **Documentation**:\\n   - Ensure the docstring is updated to reflect the implementation details and examples.\\n\\n10. **Complexity**:\\n\\n   - The median sorting step takes O(n log n) time and O(n) extra space; the subsequent deviation scan is linear.\\n\\n"}'}]
